<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karl Günther, Prince of Schwarzburg-Sondershausen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1830">1830</a>–<a href="/years/1909">1909</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karl Günther was the last Prince of Schwarzburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sondershausen">Sondershausen</a>, reigning from 1880 until his death. A conservative ruler of a small Thuringian state within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>, he died without children, and the principality passed in personal union to his kinsman Günther Victor of Schwarzburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolstadt">Rudolstadt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karl-gunther-prince-of-schwarzburg-sondershausen.jpg" alt="Karl Günther, Prince of Schwarzburg-Sondershausen" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Reichard &amp; Lindner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_G%C3%BCnther_von_Schwarzburg-Sondershausen,_1896.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
